@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-availability-lists-free-equipment-by-the-same-overlap-rule-as-booking
+type: decision-log
+title: "Availability lists free equipment by the same overlap rule as booking"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Context
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented. dl-003 left this open: a client that
+wants to show whether an item is free must call `book` or a separate availability query, and that
+query was not part of the module. The request asks for `availability({ start, end, kind })`, where
+`kind` is optional, returning the ids of the free equipment, sorted.
+
+The request does not say how an unknown `kind` is handled, what order the ids come in beyond
+"sorted", or whether the period is checked the same way as in `quote` and `book`.
+
+# Decision
+
+- An item is free for a period when no booking of it overlaps that period. The test is the same
+  half-open overlap rule `book` uses, so a booking that ends at midnight does not block a period that
+  starts then. The check is shared with `book`, not written twice.
+- `start` and `end` are validated exactly as in `quote` and `book`: UTC midnights, and `end` after
+  `start`. A bad period throws.
+- `kind` is optional. Omitted, the query covers all kinds. Given, it must be `'board'` or `'sail'`;
+  any other value throws, as `addEquipment` does, so a typo cannot silently return an empty list.
+- The result is the array of matching item ids, sorted in plain string order. Sorting makes the
+  output deterministic, in line with the determinism rule, and does not depend on insertion order.
+
+# Consequences
+
+- A client can show availability with one call, without trying to book.
+- The overlap rule lives in one place, so `availability` and `book` cannot disagree about what is busy.
+- The query reads the bookings as they stand at the call. It does not reserve anything, so a `book`
+  made just after can still refuse an item that the query listed as free.
+- dl-003 is not changed. Its consequence that availability is missing is resolved by this decision.
