@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+---
+id: task-002-rental-availability-query-for-free-equipment
+type: task
+title: "Rental availability query for free equipment"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is
+optional. It returns the ids of the equipment of that kind, or of any kind when none is given, that is
+free for the whole period, sorted. The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented.
+
+# Work
+
+- Tests first, in `src/rental.test.ts`: the full list sorted by id, the kind filter, overlapping and
+  boundary periods, an empty result, the query not reserving anything, and the error paths for an
+  unknown kind and a bad period. Run before the implementation, they failed to compile.
+- Implementation in `src/rental.ts`: the `availability` method, the exported `AvailabilityQuery` type,
+  and a `validateKind` helper shared with `addEquipment`. The overlap check is the one `book` uses.
+- `src/index.ts` re-exports `AvailabilityQuery`. `README.md` lists the new operation.
+- The design choices are recorded in dl-004.
+
+# Result
+
+- `npm test` builds with strict TypeScript and runs 27 tests, all passing: the 19 existing tests and 8
+  new ones.
+- Not changed: `quote`, `book` and `addEquipment` behave as before.
+- Not done: cancellations, which remain out of scope.
